HELUT EPISODE 12 — FIVE-VOTER PRIVATE MAJORITY
Captured 2026-09-04 on Apple silicon / Metal
This is a curated receipt. Full command output is under build/episode12/.

BOUNDED CLAIM
HELUT evaluates a synthesized five-input majority function on encrypted ballot bits,
decrypts the one-bit result inside the SING harness, and compares it with the clear
golden model. This is not a deployed multiparty voting protocol. The N=1024 receipt
uses the exact-noiseless boolean bootstrap-key construction; it is not a noisy-BK proof.

